---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

// `/events/` — what the club has on besides its races.
//
// **A static list, and the one link on it is a page rather than a database read.** There is
// one social today, so a list painted from `store.socials` would be a round trip to learn
// something the build already knows — and a second social needs its own content page anyway,
// which is a deploy either way. When there are enough of these to be worth a query, this is
// the page that becomes one.
//
// **It states no fact about any occasion.** The date, the venue and the price of the Christmas
// party are not confirmed, and this page deliberately does not preview any of them: a list
// that says "6 December" because last year's did is the club announcing a date it has not
// agreed. The occasion's own page reads what the database actually holds.
//
// The address is `/events/` because that is what the old Squarespace site published and Phase
// 5 keeps its paths. The schema calls this a *social*, because the glossary reserves *event*
// for one running of one race in one year — see ADR-033.
---

<Base
  title="Events — Southville Running Club"
  description="Socials, parties and other club events at Southville Running Club."
>
  <h1>Events</h1>

  <p class="lede">Club socials, parties and everything that is not a race.</p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/events/christmas-party-2026/"><strong>SRC Christmas Party 2026</strong></a
      > — details to be confirmed
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Looking for a race? <a href="/nn/">Nightingale Nightmare</a> is the club's own 10km off
    road, and entries are handled separately.
  </p>

  <footer>
    <p>Southville Running Club.</p>
  </footer>
</Base>
